# Totem

## Pre-Publication Clean-Slate Authority

Policy ID: `pre-publication-clean-slate-v1`.

- Treat this site and all systems that consume it as pre-publication dogfood, even when a development URL is publicly reachable.
- Until the human explicitly removes this authority, choose the best current architecture. Full rewrites and clean contract replacements are authorized when they improve correctness, security, maintainability, performance, accessibility, or product quality.
- Verify replacements end to end, migrate every dogfood caller to one current contract, remove superseded implementation in the same completed change, and finish tests, documentation, security review, and cleanup before deployment.
- Preserve immutable receipts and historical failure evidence as audit truth, never as a promise to support obsolete product behavior.

## Documentation Integrity Authority

- This documentation-first site is a primary product surface, not secondary collateral. Keep its architecture, protocol, schema, security, privacy, integration, operations, troubleshooting, limitation, and release material complete, technically rigorous, navigable, searchable, and current.
- Update affected documentation, examples, diagrams, API and contract references, error behavior, deployment guidance, and cross-site links in the same completed change as the implementation or contract they describe.
- Verify runnable examples, internal and external links, navigation, search discoverability, code samples, version references, accessibility, responsive rendering, and public HTTPS readback before publication.
- Distinguish proposed, implemented, locally tested, externally verified, deployed, and unavailable behavior. Never turn research, a fixture, a source commit, a package, or a reachable page into a stronger claim.
- Block publication when documentation is missing, stale, contradictory, version-skewed, or inconsistent with MiniModel.org, TinyRustLM.com, source contracts, update history, or machine-readable release records.
- Remove superseded guidance after its replacement and all consuming references are verified. Retain immutable release history and failure evidence separately; do not preserve obsolete instructions as legacy support.
